# Cadence UX loop

One agent owns the full cycle via `docs/CADENCE_UX_BACKLOG.md`. **Never stop the loop on your own.** The user ends the task when they want to.

## Cycle (repeat forever)

Each **iteration** = implement then test, back-to-back in the same session:

| Step | Do |
|------|-----|
| **1. Implement** | Fix the next **batch** (P0 all, then 3–5 related P1/P2 items). Add `→ Fix:` under each item. Build must succeed. |
| **2. Test** | Build + iPhone 16 Pro Max simulator. Run `scripts/cadence_sim_spot_check.sh` after install (screenshots all 5 tabs + Settings + global search). Also exercise flows touched by the batch. Mark verified items Done with date. |

Then **immediately** start the next iteration. Do not pause, poll, or hand off.

## When backlog is empty

Run a **fresh UX audit** (all tabs, key flows, code skim) → append new P2 batches → implement → test → repeat.

## Loop signal

Update `docs/CADENCE_UX_BACKLOG.md` each iteration (next batch, summary). **Do not set Phase to stop.** Keep `Phase: RUNNING` unless the user explicitly says to pause.

**Never:** sleep/poll loops, wait for another agent, or stop because backlog is clear — audit and add more work.

## Batches

- Work in **batches**, not one item per pass.
- Priority: P0 → P1 → P2 (A, B, C… groups in backlog).

## App

After any light-mode test, restore dark: `xcrun simctl ui … appearance dark` (Cadence is dark-first).
